<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    The factions tab, with the standing drawn against the band it rests in.

    order 90, validWithoutMap and minimized are vanilla's own, so the button sits exactly where it always
    did for a player whose bar falls back to the game's ordering. The tab is worth reading from the world
    view, which is what validWithoutMap buys: a standing is a fact about the planet, not about a map.

    The hotkey is not restated here because vanilla's def carries none.
    Patch_MainTabsRoot_ToggleTab_Factions catches the toggle and sends it here, which is also how the info
    card's "show me this faction" and the pawn table's faction icon arrive at our tab.

    The icon is the one already in this mod's own UI/MainButtonIcons folder, so the glyph on the bar and
    the mark at the top of the tab are the same drawing.
  -->
  <MainButtonDef>
    <defName>Gideon_Factions</defName>
    <label>factions</label>
    <description>Every faction on the planet and where you stand with each one. A standing is drawn against the band it settles in, so a faction that is being pulled back toward neutral is told apart from one that is simply where it belongs. Opening a faction says what is holding its standing down, what the resting value is made of, and what you did this year that moved it.</description>
    <tabWindowClass>Gideon.UIOverhaul.Features.Factions.MainTabWindow_Factions</tabWindowClass>
    <order>90</order>
    <validWithoutMap>true</validWithoutMap>
    <minimized>True</minimized>
    <iconPath>UI/MainButtonIcons/Factions</iconPath>
  </MainButtonDef>

</Defs>
